      "status": "affected",
      "action_statement": "Update nodejs-24 to 24.22.3-0 or later.",
      "status_notes": "CVE-2026-123871: Node.js puts the raw proxy URL, including any username and password, into ERR_PROXY_INVALID_CONFIG error messages on four error paths of its built-in HTTP proxy support that the earlier fix for CVE-2026-48615 missed, so proxy credentials taken from the environment can be written to stderr, container logs, log aggregation or crash reports. The November 2026 security advisory lists the 22.x, 24.x and 26.x lines as affected (https://nodejs.org/en/blog/vulnerability/november-2026-security-releases), and Node.js fixed 24.x in 24.22.3 (https://github.com/nodejs/node/releases/tag/v24.22.3) with https://github.com/nodejs/node/commit/8749030ae5 (http: redact proxy credentials in invalid proxy URL errors), which carries this CVE id and is not in 24.22.2. We read the version string from the node binary in every published nodejs-24 package for Debian 13 in the DHI Debian repository (24.16.0-0 to the current 24.22.3-0, amd64 and arm64); each matches its package version, so builds below 24.22.3-0 ship Node.js 24.22.2 or older and 24.22.3-0, the current build, ships 24.22.3. The range ends at 24.22.3-0, the first build with the fix."
